      "content": "I'm very sorry that you're going through this. You should immediately run the burn under cool (not cold) water for at least 10-20 minutes to reduce the temperature and pain. After that, apply a cool, clean cloth loosely covering the burn to reduce skin sensitivity. Do not apply any oils or butter directly to the burn, as this could trap heat and increase the risk of infection. Keep the area clean and exposed to the air, and consider using antibiotic ointment to prevent infection. Seek medical attention promptly for further assessment and treatment. Avoid covering the burn with non-breathable materials like bandages.",
